{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral","id":1024400,"title":"Dancing with the spiral","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-30T10:48:23-08:00","id":1024400,"title":"Dancing with the spiral","content":"So yet again my google fu has failed me, is there any recent books (revised or more) that explains what happens when you dance with the spiral in its entirety or is it a GM fiat type of deal? Also, what happens if a kinfolk were to dance with the spiral and survive (unlikely I know because of the not being able to heal easily part, but certainly the mental trials would be no different right?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","name":"Asssassin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T11:29:14-08:00","id":1024421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asssassin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral#post1024400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yet again my google fu has failed me, is there any recent books (revised or more) that explains what happens when you dance with the spiral in its entirety or is it a GM fiat type of deal? Also, what happens if a kinfolk were to dance with the spiral and survive (unlikely I know because of the not being able to heal easily part, but certainly the mental trials would be no different right?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Dancing the Spiral, as a Garou or Fera, is an instant and complete SAN-blasting. You're wholly corrupted, and possibly not very cogent anymore. It's a hand in your character sheet kind of deal.<br /> <br /> Kin don't have the spiritual or physical fortitude to dance it, and the mental trials are no less above a human's capability, on account of how they probably take longer than humans can manage with their merely human Stamina. That, and the rite only leads changers down. Humans and wolves are at the mercy of spiritual beings that will probably eat them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T14:31:02-08:00","id":1024501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1024421#post1024421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dancing the Spiral, as a Garou or Fera, is an instant and complete SAN-blasting. You're wholly corrupted, and possibly not very cogent anymore. It's a hand in your character sheet kind of deal.<br /> <br /> Kin don't have the spiritual or physical fortitude to dance it, and the mental trials are no less above a human's capability, on account of how they probably take longer than humans can manage with their merely human Stamina. That, and the rite only leads changers down. Humans and wolves are at the mercy of spiritual beings that will probably eat them.</div> </div> </div> </div>what about a mage with high life and spirit and such who is a kinfolk to the spirals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","name":"Asssassin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T17:07:16-08:00","id":1024569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asssassin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1024501#post1024501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> what about a mage with high life and spirit and such who is a kinfolk to the spirals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then it counts as entering a Caul and the mage becomes your everyday, pedestrian Nephandus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T18:21:35-08:00","id":1024597,"title":"","content":"I think the most explanation you get from the rule books (not sure about the novels) that isn't ST-fiat is that <i>if you survive</i>, you become an Agent (capital A to distinguish from 'merely' becoming corrupt) of the Wyrm in some capacity, which may or may leave you playable (if a PC). This is what happened to the Nightmaster, who thought he could dance his way right to the Wyrm and kill it, and ended up with an officer's commission in its army, instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T20:29:04-08:00","id":1024610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yakecen-Sings</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1024597#post1024597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the most explanation you get from the rule books (not sure about the novels) that isn't ST-fiat is that <i>if you survive</i>, you become an Agent (capital A to distinguish from 'merely' becoming corrupt) of the Wyrm in some capacity, which may or may leave you playable (if a PC). This is what happened to the Nightmaster, who thought he could dance his way right to the Wyrm and kill it, and ended up with an officer's commission in its army, instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't Nightmaster go into the Abyss Realm instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T22:04:09-08:00","id":1024634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1024610#post1024610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't Nightmaster go into the Abyss Realm instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2810_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2810\" data-vbnamecard=\"2810\">Yakecen-Sings</a> is thinking of Hakaken I believe.<br /> <br /> But yea, to the OP: dancing the Spiral leaves you as an NPC if you survive. And your Spheres don't save you. You're going against a Supernal. (Assuming Werewolf cosmology). So either dead, or corrupt NPC. Neither option is good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 12-31-2016, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T00:16:28-08:00","id":1024648,"title":"","content":"Oop, my bad. I conflated the two since they're both Shadow Lords. Honestly, Nightmaster <i>may as well</i> have Danced the Spiral at this point in all but formality. But yes, I meant Hakaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T01:28:35-08:00","id":1024665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asssassin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral#post1024400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, what happens if a kinfolk were to dance with the spiral and survive (unlikely I know because of the not being able to heal easily part, but certainly the mental trials would be no different right?)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1024569#post1024569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then it counts as entering a Caul and the mage becomes your everyday, pedestrian Nephandus.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 mentions that a Sleeper can Awaken if they go into a Caul. Thus, perhaps a Kinfolk (and non-Kinfolk) could become a Malfean Nephandi by Dancing the Black Spiral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T06:49:09-08:00","id":1024741,"title":"","content":"Either way, you are an NPC. Dancing the spiral brought down an entire Garou Tribe and has probably been the end of many a proud Mage. It is a one way trip and no one comes back sane and uncorrupted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T07:50:08-08:00","id":1024758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1024741#post1024741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Dancing the spiral brought down an entire Garou Tribe and has probably been the end of many a proud Mage. It is a one way trip and no one comes back sane and uncorrupted.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Lost Paths</i> mentions that Ahl-i-Batin, due to their use of labyrinths for enlightenment, disagreed with the notion of the Black Spiral corrupting them. Of those who tried to test the notion, half became Barrabi, many become catatonic, a small handful disappeared upon reaching the center, and the rest became spies among the Nephandi.<br /> This gives Ahl-i-Batin the dubious honor of being a group of Mages with a unique reason for Falling: &quot;I wanted to prove that I can't Fall.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T08:03:09-08:00","id":1024760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1024665#post1024665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> M20 mentions that a Sleeper can Awaken if they go into a Caul. Thus, perhaps a Kinfolk (and non-Kinfolk) could become a Malfean Nephandi by Dancing the Black Spiral.</div> </div> </div> </div>But probably not. It'd be way too easy to manufacture Nephandi, otherwise, since cultists could just go around throwing people into Cauls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T08:15:51-08:00","id":1024764,"title":"","content":"Or just walk the Spiral themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T09:12:11-08:00","id":1024781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1024764#post1024764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or just walk the Spiral themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is assuming that they've already come back from their trip and are looking for fresh meat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T09:45:24-08:00","id":1024792,"title":"","content":"It would be worth it to cultists even if only 1% of the people survived because 100 innocents dying is a cheap price for 1 Nephandi. The success rate would have to be 0.01% or lower, as it would be too time consuming and difficult to toss 10,000 people in to just get 1 Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T18:36:36-08:00","id":1024964,"title":"","content":"Oh wow...fair enough. Our group allows for us to play usually NPC style games as we have been gaming for over 15 years and know how to not be ridiculous about it, that being said, Being an agent of the wyrm in my eyes is no different than being an agent of the weaver or the wyld, and yet they are allowed as pc's all the time. You just get &quot;take over&quot; from time to time when the Celestine or whatever you wanna call it, needs you. Can be a bad time if youre with the group, but then again that depends on the GM...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","name":"Asssassin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T18:54:21-08:00","id":1024970,"title":"","content":"That is a little odd, but whatever works for you. While I have occasionally had games where the players were (or were allied to) fomori, they (and their allies) were never agents of the Wyrm. They were victims of the Wyrm who devoted themselves to opposing the forces of the Wyrm that had ruined their lives.<br /> <br /> I do not think that it is good to have a mixed group of people who work for the Wyrm, Wyld, and Weaver, as they should be killing each other with extreme prejudice. In the case of the Ananasi, they are associated with the members of the Triat, but they are all double agents who are working with their Queen, so it is more about being effective double agents than anything else. In the case of the other Fera, everyone should be agents of Gaia and any group that allies with a member of the Triat over Gaia (like the Black Spiral Dancers, the Kumo, or the Ratkin) should be considered to be the enemies of Gaia because they have abandoned their duties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 12-31-2016, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T20:21:16-08:00","id":1024989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asssassin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1024964#post1024964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh wow...fair enough. Our group allows for us to play usually NPC style games as we have been gaming for over 15 years and know how to not be ridiculous about it, that being said, Being an agent of the wyrm in my eyes is no different than being an agent of the weaver or the wyld, and yet they are allowed as pc's all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they actually usually aren't. At least, not beyond Drones or Gorgons, and fomori fit in with them. Greater agents of those powers, not so much. Being bound to any one member of the Triat is not good for self-agency.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You just get &quot;take over&quot; from time to time when the Celestine or whatever you wanna call it, needs you. Can be a bad time if youre with the group, but then again that depends on the GM... </div> </div> </div>That seems way too easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T11:44:25-08:00","id":1025125,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that Nightmaster has no connection to the Spiral or the Wyrm. He's utterly &quot;mad&quot; but is still very much a Shadowlord and master of the Society of Nidhogg and he originally wanted to devour Helios bu that ambition extended to Anthelios when it showed up too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T12:46:33-08:00","id":1025135,"title":"","content":"Have we ever gotten more infortmation on the Nightmaster anywhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T14:44:02-08:00","id":1025170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1024989#post1024989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they actually usually aren't. At least, not beyond Drones or Gorgons, and fomori fit in with them. Greater agents of those powers, not so much. Being bound to any one member of the Triat is not good for self-agency.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That seems way too easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in like making any other deal you negotiate the terms in our eyes. So maybe not getting the full on power suite and being more fomorish = the only take over at certain times issue. Not to say its something that wouldn't come up and fuck up your night. I mean our GM isn't like a nice one, it is the WOD afterall. It just wouldn't be all the time type of deal. So, you and your coterie have a mission to do for a prince or something, oops looks like the wyrm needs you tonight, and maybe to fight off your allies...is an absolute possibility, but not something that will happen on a night to night basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","name":"Asssassin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T18:21:43-08:00","id":1025222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asssassin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1025170#post1025170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well in like making any other deal you negotiate the terms in our eyes. So maybe not getting the full on power suite and being more fomorish = the only take over at certain times issue. Not to say its something that wouldn't come up and fuck up your night. I mean our GM isn't like a nice one, it is the WOD afterall. It just wouldn't be all the time type of deal. So, you and your coterie have a mission to do for a prince or something, oops looks like the wyrm needs you tonight, and maybe to fight off your allies...is an absolute possibility, but not something that will happen on a night to night basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you adapted the lesser akuma system from KotE?<br /> <br /> The Wyld and Weaver would be having you do the same, in that case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T19:01:46-08:00","id":1025233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1025135#post1025135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have we ever gotten more infortmation on the Nightmaster anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Umbra, the Abyss section is the only place I know of off the top of my head. I feel like there's at least one other place, but I can't remember where, if so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T19:42:46-08:00","id":1025243,"title":"","content":"Isn't Nightmaster in Shattered Dreams...? Or does it not present any new information?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T07:41:45-08:00","id":1025428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1025243#post1025243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Nightmaster in Shattered Dreams...? Or does it not present any new information?</div> </div> </div> </div>He's an antagonist filling a role in a story that's been labeled non-canonical, so any details would not technically be applicable if they were there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T08:28:20-08:00","id":1025451,"title":"","content":"Books that include spiral dancing fun: all books of the wyrm to varying degrees, and I would include mind's eye book of the wyrm second. For short stories eyes towards heaven is a spiral related tale, but Trinity caern is the take all of spiral dancing. <br /> <br /> Dancing the spiral mechanically may not drive you insane. There's a chance you could roll well enough and walk out of there not crazy. Well... Not anymore then you would have to be to want to be there in the first place. I'm talking serial killers and the like. Course it could just end up like the silver fangs in a tribe falls where they just decide it's time to end the world.<br /> <br /> At any rate, dancing the spiral in no way has to be a hand over the character sheet moment, and I'm very much pro playing the bad guy. It largely depends on your gm and your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T08:40:51-08:00","id":1025456,"title":"","content":"We are not talking about playing the bad guy. You can play an Infernalist without trouble in any of the gamelines (though the Infernalist who end up Bane-Possessed, Demon-thralls, or Specter-cultists end up with the short end of the stick). It is about playing characters whose motivations are now so alien that no human player is capable of understanding them without going insane. Since human player could possible play them making them into a farce, STs make the character into an NPC to preserve the integrity of the game. That is why I think that Baali, Black Spiral Dancers, Demons, Nephandi, Specters, etc should allow be NPCs, because no human can play them right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T09:05:52-08:00","id":1025465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1025456#post1025456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are not talking about playing the bad guy. You can play an Infernalist without trouble in any of the gamelines (though the Infernalist who end up Bane-Possessed, Demon-thralls, or Specter-cultists end up with the short end of the stick). It is about playing characters whose motivations are now so alien that no human player is capable of understanding them without going insane. Since human player could possible play them making them into a farce, STs make the character into an NPC to preserve the integrity of the game. That is why I think that Baali, Black Spiral Dancers, Demons, Nephandi, Specters, etc should allow be NPCs, because no human can play them right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you vastly underestimate the ability of humans to do things. Just because you haven't seen it done or something doesn't mean it cannot be done. I mean why have roads in Vamp then? They are all foreign ideas that &quot;humans&quot; could never grasp right? That's just asinine thinking in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","name":"Asssassin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T10:57:04-08:00","id":1025494,"title":"","content":"I have seen hundreds of people try to play the 'chaotic evil' characters that you are talking about over the past quarter century and, regardless of the region, they always end up playing 'chaotic stupid' rather than 'chaotic evil'. The 'lawful evil' equivalents (Infernalists, Sabbat, etc) are doable because we only need look at corporations, governments, religions, and syndicates to gain plenty of examples in real life. Even 'neutral evil' has plenty of real world examples in everyday criminals and historical examples such as the Mongols and the Nazis. The only examples of 'chaotic evil' in real life are serial killers and, as someone who has studied them for professional research, few people without proper training are capable of looking in that Abyss without becoming strange.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T12:35:51-08:00","id":1025527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1025494#post1025494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have seen hundreds of people try to play the 'chaotic evil' characters that you are talking about over the past quarter century and, regardless of the region, they always end up playing 'chaotic stupid' rather than 'chaotic evil'. The 'lawful evil' equivalents (Infernalists, Sabbat, etc) are doable because we only need look at corporations, governments, religions, and syndicates to gain plenty of examples in real life. Even 'neutral evil' has plenty of real world examples in everyday criminals and historical examples such as the Mongols and the Nazis. The only examples of 'chaotic evil' in real life are serial killers and, as someone who has studied them for professional research, few people without proper training are capable of looking in that Abyss without becoming strange.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in what way were we saying that this would make you a CE type character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","name":"Asssassin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T13:13:04-08:00","id":1025537,"title":"","content":"What else do you call the Black Spiral Dancers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T13:19:36-08:00","id":1025540,"title":"","content":"BSD may be chaotic evil, but not so much the Baali, Nephandi or Demons. Those groups are much looser, and capable of being the long-term plotters and planners (LE), acting mostly spur-of-the-moment in their depravity (CE) or switching between the two as needed and as it will most benefit them (NE).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T13:30:31-08:00","id":1025546,"title":"","content":"I disagree that a character who has gone through the Spiral can't be played because of human limitation. Humans conceived of all these concepts; we can reckon them. I think it's more about, at that point how to do play them without making the other players involved really uncomfortable (the 'should you' aspect of it) + how do you justify the character who has gone through this experience still getting up to relatively mundane things, and not, say, focusing on taking over a Realm. If a ST can do justice to NPC bad guys that have been deemed not suitable for PCs because they are too alien to understand, then what makes a ST so supernatural that they can understand and portray them properly? Or is it really just roleplaying chops?<br /> <br /> Mechanically, the insanity isn't really enforced. But I think if you look at purely the mechanics, you're doing a disservice to the concept/setting and yourself, just like in any situation where you look at only the numbers and not the spirit of it, especially in a game like Werewolf. You have to change in order to progress through each circle of the Labyrinth. It's even called the Rite of Transmogrification. You can't just coast through it unscathed; you have to become damaged, deformed, different in order to make it through and glean those fell insights. By the time you've somehow made it through all nine circles, you're so <i>different </i>and <i>changed </i>from how you were before you started, you're probably not much of the same character anymore. If I'm not conflating things again, Hakaken is depicted as being a crab-monster since he Danced his way to being a Wyrm Incarna. He's not even Garou anymore, nevermind the psychological changes.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, though, once the character has gone through the Labyrinth, is it doing justice to the extreme changes, the paradigm shift (capital P, if you prefer) and whatnot of the experience that they remain in play as a PC? If you can, and the game is one where that makes sense and the rest of the troupe is good with it, then it has the potential to work. But it's a lot of circumstances that need to align that usually don't, which is why the default answer is &quot;nah, hand your sheet to the ST&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T06:01:54-08:00","id":1025878,"title":"","content":"(Note, I've played a lot of Exalted so this may skew my views.)<br /> <br /> I don't think Dancing the Spiral is an instant &quot;You are of the Wyrm now!&quot; for a PC. The White Howlers did it before and, while it did get their tribe in the end, generations of them made it though before that happened. And a PC is a cut above all the run of the mill NPCs out there, so if anyone is going to dance the spiral and keep their loyalty to Gaia, it's going to be a PC.<br /> <br /> There is going to be consequences. You are going to be changed. Maybe kind of crazy. No one is going to trust you. You may be harassed by banes, tempting you to fall to the Wyrm. Your pack may have to go on the run until you can prove to the Garou Nation that you aren't a Black Spiral Dancer. The Black Spiral Dancer may want you dead, because your character just proved the &quot;No one can survive the spiral and not be of the Wyrm&quot; wrong.<br /> <br /> But that sounds like awesome plot to play though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T09:52:42-08:00","id":1025994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1025878#post1025878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think Dancing the Spiral is an instant &quot;You are of the Wyrm now!&quot; for a PC. The White Howlers did it before and, while it did get their tribe in the end, generations of them made it though before that happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe this got retconned, but as the story is currently presented, the Howlers found the entrance to the Spiral and after some deliberation, jumped in as an entire Tribe. They had not been making individual forays into it prior to their fall. <br /> <br /> I don't know if that means 'instant corruption,' but I think it is likely that like Malfeas, you only leave when allowed to, and that will only happen when corruption is complete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:02:49-08:00","id":1025999,"title":"","content":"So I don't think Spirals should be off limits for roleplaying at all, it really just depends on the game being run. There is nothing inherently unknowable about playing a corrupt character (Spiral, Nephandi, Baali, etc.). And for the person that said Spirals are the D&amp;D Chaotic Evil equivalent, I would point out that they can and do follow a (fairly) rigid litany. CE doesn't do that. But really, D7D alignments have zero place in the WoD and they aren't even good for comparisons.<br /> <br /> So I do think you can dance the Spiral and be a PC. But if the game was a Gaian game prior to one PC dancing the Spiral, I find it most appropriate to have the character be removed to NPC status. That's just how I would handle it.<br /> <br /> Now, if a character theoretically danced to the end of the Spiral, then they really need to be an NPC. The only canon examples we have are elevated entities (Hakaken, the Wyrm totem) that have little in common with a PC character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:04:07-08:00","id":1026000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1025994#post1025994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe this got retconned, but as the story is currently presented, the Howlers found the entrance to the Spiral and after some deliberation, jumped in as an entire Tribe. They had not been making individual forays into it prior to their fall.<br /> <br /> I don't know if that means 'instant corruption,' but I think it is likely that like Malfeas, you only leave when allowed to, and that will only happen when corruption is complete.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I vaguely remember something about the White Howlers using Dancing the Spiral as a rite of passage. Eventually the whispers of the Wyrm got to the tribe and the fell.<br /> <br /> I think I got that story from another tribe's splat book (Fianna?) and the moral of the story was &quot;Don't be arrogant about the Wyrm.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:07:01-08:00","id":1026002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1025994#post1025994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if that means 'instant corruption,' but I think it is likely that like Malfeas, you only leave when allowed to, and that will only happen when corruption is complete.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree that the point isn't 'you enter the Labrinth and now you are instantly insane.' The process of dancing the labrinth is what results in that state. But if you've truly danced the spiral and exerpienced it fully, you are absolutely twisted into a dancer. I think it kind of devalues the horror if someone could dance it and also holds their core beliefs/morality/etc. Redemption of a dancer is quite different than just outright resisting the place.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:13:39-08:00","id":1026007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1026002#post1026002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I agree that the point isn't 'you enter the Labrinth and now you are instantly insane.' The process of dancing the labrinth is what results in that state. But if you've truly danced the spiral and exerpienced it fully, you are absolutely twisted into a dancer. I think it kind of devalues the horror if someone could dance it and also holds their core beliefs/morality/etc. Redemption of a dancer is quite different than just outright resisting the place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm going to drop my point, as I have played too much Exalted and forget that WoD doesn't have Integrity as a Ability. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:57:46-08:00","id":1026047,"title":"","content":"I think that the misunderstanding here is caused by STs not requiring players to roleplay the evil actions that their characters commit. It is easy for a player to say that their character is skinning kittens, impaling infants, raping nuns, etc., it is another thing for them to roleplay the events with the ST, in front of the other players, where they will be implicitly judged by the group. It is easy to be play evil when you do not have to roleplay evil.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:42:18-08:00","id":1026082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1026047#post1026047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the misunderstanding here is caused by STs not requiring players to roleplay the evil actions that their characters commit. It is easy for a player to say that their character is skinning kittens, impaling infants, raping nuns, etc., it is another thing for them to roleplay the events with the ST, in front of the other players, where they will be implicitly judged by the group. It is easy to be play evil when you do not have to roleplay evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think conflating senseless violence with these evil groups is the misunderstanding. Book of the Wyrm gives a fair bit of information of Black Spiral Dancer motivations and their delusional justifications. Which doesn't necessarily include random crimes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T12:12:22-08:00","id":1026101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1026047#post1026047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think that the misunderstanding here is caused by STs not requiring players to roleplay the evil actions that their characters commit. It is easy for a player to say that their character is skinning kittens, impaling infants, raping nuns, etc., it is another thing for them to roleplay the events with the ST, in front of the other players, where they will be implicitly judged by the group. It is easy to be play evil when you do not have to roleplay evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>So while these sort of things aren't against any moral codes (generally), what purpose do they serve? That's a sticking point I have with these examples. So called &quot;evil&quot; characters (again, Spirals, Baali, Nephandi, etc.) don't run around doing these things. Not without very specific reasons. Spirals aren't running around raping nuns for laughs. Like the Garou, they have better things to do then get randomly sidetracked, especially for the sake of mustache twirling evilness.<br /> <br /> And I don't see what your point is, with whether or not this sort of thing happens on screen is. Does that make a difference?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T16:07:18-08:00","id":1026198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1026101#post1026101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while these sort of things aren't against any moral codes (generally), what purpose do they serve? That's a sticking point I have with these examples. So called &quot;evil&quot; characters (again, Spirals, Baali, Nephandi, etc.) don't run around doing these things. Not without very specific reasons. Spirals aren't running around raping nuns for laughs. Like the Garou, they have better things to do then get randomly sidetracked, especially for the sake of mustache twirling evilness.<br /> <br /> And I don't see what your point is, with whether or not this sort of thing happens on screen is. Does that make a difference?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the way I always saw it is, we have an idea that we believe in, and although human sacrifice and nun raping may be a thing that we use to fuel our wyrm filled rituals, it isn't something they do every single minute of every single day while they cackle manically and what not. Otherwise, towns of humans near them would root them out and just kill them. I mean honestly. The OMG suzie went missing while traveling in the Louisiana boyou, as compared to OMG that whole town just disappeared in one night, will have drastically different responses, by government and otherwise, and in the WOD that breaks your stuff and kills you. They are evil, and will do evil, terrible things, but they don't do it without purpose.<br /> <br /> and just to point out, insanity is defined as doing the same thing over and over and expecting different results. So in the most literal terms, everyone in the WOD (clan, paradigm, pack theme..whatever have you) defines you in some way, and you use that way to exist or die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","user":"Asssassin","date":". 01-03-2017, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","name":"Asssassin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T18:30:52-08:00","id":1026253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asssassin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1026198#post1026198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah the way I always saw it is, we have an idea that we believe in, and although human sacrifice and nun raping may be a thing that we use to fuel our wyrm filled rituals, it isn't something they do every single minute of every single day while they cackle manically and what not. Otherwise, towns of humans near them would root them out and just kill them. I mean honestly. The OMG suzie went missing while traveling in the Louisiana boyou, as compared to OMG that whole town just disappeared in one night, will have drastically different responses, by government and otherwise, and in the WOD that breaks your stuff and kills you. They are evil, and will do evil, terrible things, but they don't do it without purpose.<br /> <br /> and just to point out, insanity is defined as doing the same thing over and over and expecting different results. So in the most literal terms, everyone in the WOD (clan, paradigm, pack theme..whatever have you) defines you in some way, and you use that way to exist or die.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the first paragraph. Nitpick on the second. That is very much not the definition of insanity. That is a quote from Einstein. And while he was brilliant man, his fields had nothing to do with either psychology or linguistics. The fact that that &quot;definition&quot; is so often quoted is actually kind of annoying. And admittedly, this is just a personal statement with no impact on the greater discussion at hand. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T09:12:39-08:00","id":1026557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1024400-dancing-with-the-spiral?p=1025994#post1025994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe this got retconned, but as the story is currently presented, the Howlers found the entrance to the Spiral and after some deliberation, jumped in as an entire Tribe. They had not been making individual forays into it prior to their fall.<br /> <br /> I don't know if that means 'instant corruption,' but I think it is likely that like Malfeas, you only leave when allowed to, and that will only happen when corruption is complete.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can get out of Malfeas without being &quot;let out&quot;, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[